WEBVTT

00:00:07.426 --> 00:00:10.842
A supply bin must never issue more items than it

00:00:10.842 --> 00:00:11.269
holds.

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:14.970
Encapsulation keeps its state behind operations that

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.108
control changes.

00:00:16.108 --> 00:00:19.026
We start each bin with nonnegative stock.

00:00:45.319 --> 00:00:48.719
Private fields cannot be changed directly by this

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:49.204
caller.

00:00:49.204 --> 00:00:51.286
Public methods provide access.

00:00:51.286 --> 00:00:54.755
The take method rejects a nonpositive or excessive

00:00:54.755 --> 00:00:56.836
request before changing stock.

00:00:56.836 --> 00:01:00.444
That protects the rule that stock stays nonnegative.

00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:02.685
Each bin has its own stock.

00:01:02.685 --> 00:01:06.488
The static binsCreated field belongs to the class, and

00:01:06.488 --> 00:01:09.657
the constructor updates it for every new bin.

00:01:09.657 --> 00:01:13.460
Trace both take calls and predict all five lines, then

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:13.883
pause.

00:01:18.795 --> 00:01:21.483
Taking three succeeds, leaving two pens.

00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:24.575
Taking four fails without changing that stock.

00:01:24.575 --> 00:01:26.389
The maps bin still has two.

00:01:26.389 --> 00:01:29.414
The shared count is two because two bins were

00:01:29.414 --> 00:01:30.220
constructed.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.464
Change the second request and its printed label to

00:01:33.464 --> 00:01:34.040
take two.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.575
Predict the new results.

00:01:35.575 --> 00:01:38.772
Why do the maps stock and the class count stay the

00:01:38.772 --> 00:01:39.092
same?
